<p>Use the following procedure to print on both sides of sheets using a 
 layout suitable for booklets.</p>
<p>Two formats are available. </p>
<p><span class="Term-Soft">Magazine</span>: the whole stack is folded in 
 half in a similar way to a magazine.</p>
<p><span class="Term-Soft">Mini Book</span>: each sheet is folded in half 
 separately, and then the folded sheets are stacked and bound.</p>
<p>The pages of your document will be reduced in size and printed side 
 by side, two on each side of each sheet of the original paper size specified 
 in the application. For example, an A4 document will be printed as two 
 A5 images on each side of each A4 sheet. Similarly a Letter size document 
 will be printed as two 5.5" x 8.5" images on each side of each 
 Letter size sheet. The whole stack is folded in half, like a magazine.</p>
<p>If you use the <span class="Term-Soft">Booklet</span> function and the 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Layout</span> function together, you will be able 
 to reduce the printing cost.</p>
<p>Depending on the printer you are using, this function may not be available.</p>
<p>Magazine: <img alt="" class="help-img" height="84" loading="lazy" src="~/images/help/MagRight.gif" width="81"/> Mini Book: <img alt="" class="help-img" height="82" loading="lazy" src="~/images/help/DuplexMiniLeft.gif" width="87"/></p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Depending on the printer you are using, it is 
 required that the duplex unit be installed.</p></li>
<li><p>To print at the same as the original without size 
 reduction, select a paper size that is double that of the original in 
 the <span class="Term-Soft">Print On:</span> list on the <span class="Term-Soft">Basic</span> 
 menu.<br/>
 You can also specify it on the <span class="Term-Soft">Basic</span> menu 
 of the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 creating a document in an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used 
 Settings</span> tab or the <span class="Term-Soft">2 Sided/Layout/Booklet</span> 
 menu of the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select <span class="Term-Soft">Magazine</span> or 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Mini Book</span> in the <span class="Term-Soft">Booklet:</span> 
 list.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p class="Normal-indent">Click the <span class="Term-Soft">&lt;&lt; Collapse list</span> button if the <span class="Term-Soft">Booklet:</span> 
 list on the <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used Settings</span> tab 
 is not displayed.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="4">
<li><p>Select a page layout in the <span class="Term-Soft">Page 
 Order:</span> list.</p></li>
<li><p>Configure the <button aria-controls="dropdown-1" aria-expanded="false" class="help-dropdown-toggle" data-bs-target="#dropdown-1" data-bs-toggle="collapse" type="button">setting for printing 
 mixed orientation documents</button> 
 and if necessary, select a layout type in the <span class="Term-Soft">Layout:</span> list, or select the <a href="~/Topics/IDH_DDUPLEX#nonreduction"><span class="Term-Soft">Do not [Fit to Print Size] auto.</span></a> check box.</p><div class="collapse help-dropdown" id="dropdown-1">
<ol>
<li><p>Open the <span class="Term-Soft">2 Sided/Layout/Booklet</span> 
 menu of the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab if the 
 <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used Settings</span> tab is displayed.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Mixed Original 
 Orientations...</span> button to open the dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<ul>
<li><p>For <span class="Term-Soft">Rotate 
 Mixed Original Orientation</span> of the <span class="Term-Soft">Output 
 Settings</span> menu, select <span class="Term-Soft">Printer Defaults</span>.</p></li>
</ul>
</div>
<ol start="3">
<li><p>Specify whether to print document pages whose 
 orientation differs from the paper orientation rotated by 90 degrees or 
 reduced in size without being rotated.</p></li>
<li><p>Click <span class="Term-Soft">OK</span> to close 
 the dialog box.</p></li>
</ol>
</div></li>
</ol>
<div class="help-step-extra">
<p class="Normal-ol"><a href="~/Topics/IDH_HOW_LAYOUT">Printing Multiple Pages 
 on a Sheet</a></p>
</div>
<ol start="6">
<li><p>If you select <span class="Term-Soft">Magazine</span>, 
 configure <a href="~/Topics/IDH_DDUPLEX#creep"><span class="Term-Soft">Creep 
 Adjustment...</span></a> if necessary. 
 </p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
